{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_rebalance", "label": "Shard rebalance", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Work-shedding, not work-acquiring: an idle node receives newly allocated shards but does not get existing ones moved into it just because it is quiet.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/rebalance.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_handoff", "label": "Handoff sequence", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Intentionally conservative - buffered messages wait for HandOffComplete before forwarding, so nothing races past a half-moved entity.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/rebalance.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_region_stopping_trigger", "label": "Region-stopping rebalance trigger", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Without it a stopped region left its shards orphaned: the coordinator kept naming it as their home, senders cached that home and delivered into a stopped actor, and nothing recovered it because the candidate set is derived from the registry with no liveness check. The notification is best-effort and idempotent - skipped without a coordinator, swallowed on transport failure, and a no-op when MemberRemoved arrives after it.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/rebalance.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_handoff_authorization", "label": "Who may order a handoff", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A HandOff stops every entity in a shard, so the region checks the peer the connection was authenticated as - never a field out of the payload - and that it is the node currently believed to host the coordinator. Until this rule existed any peer completing the handshake could take a shard's entities down repeatably. Refusing is safe because a region re-registers and re-asks on the next leader or membership event. It is authorization, not authentication: without peer certificates any party reaching the port can become a member and then the leader.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/rebalance.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_force_reallocation", "label": "Force-reallocation and orphan entities", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "If HandOffComplete does not arrive within handOffTimeoutMs the coordinator force-reallocates, and the old entities may still be alive on the source - split-brain entities until the orphans die. Causes are a hanging postStop or a partition during handoff, so keep postStop short or raise the timeout.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/rebalance.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_buffered_messages", "label": "Buffered messages during handoff", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Delayed, not dropped, and the buffer is unbounded so it can grow under load. The re-ask matters more than it looks: completing a handoff clears the old region's cached home and the coordinator only announces to the new owner and to regions with an outstanding query, so without asking a shard that goes quiet would sit on its buffer indefinitely.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/rebalance.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_rebalance", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_handoff", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/rebalance.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_handoff", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_buffered_messages", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/rebalance.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_region_stopping_trigger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_rebalance", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/rebalance.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_handoff_authorization", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_handoff", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/rebalance.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_force_reallocation", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_handoff", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/rebalance.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_rebalance_rebalance", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_allocation_strategy_allocationstrategy", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/rebalance.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "do